1
00:00:00,709 --> 00:00:02,211
[mysterious music]

2
00:00:02,294 --> 00:00:04,796
[air whooshes]

3
00:00:06,173 --> 00:00:08,091
Huh, an invitation

4
00:00:08,175 --> 00:00:10,302
to the Tournament
of the Sources?

5
00:00:10,385 --> 00:00:13,222
[laughing] Oh, yeah!

6
00:00:14,139 --> 00:00:16,683
[air whooshes]

7
00:00:16,767 --> 00:00:20,270
-Whoo!
-[mysterious music]

8
00:00:20,354 --> 00:00:21,688
[block thuds]

9
00:00:21,772 --> 00:00:24,107
[mysterious music]

10
00:00:27,486 --> 00:00:29,530
[dragons screeching]

11
00:00:29,613 --> 00:00:30,572
[scroll thuds]

12
00:00:30,656 --> 00:00:32,616
[mysterious music]

13
00:00:32,699 --> 00:00:34,993
[dragons screeching]

14
00:00:35,077 --> 00:00:36,662
[engine humming]

15
00:00:36,745 --> 00:00:39,998
[suspenseful music]

16
00:00:42,376 --> 00:00:43,836
[sniffs]

17
00:00:43,919 --> 00:00:45,337
[flowers crunch]

18
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:48,423
[suspenseful music]

19
00:00:48,507 --> 00:00:50,217
[dragons screeching]

20
00:00:55,472 --> 00:00:57,140
[dragons screeching]

21
00:01:12,281 --> 00:01:14,366
-[Ninja slurps]
-[cup clinks]

22
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:15,742
[mysterious music]

23
00:01:15,826 --> 00:01:17,661
-[air whooshes]
-[scroll thuds]

24
00:01:17,744 --> 00:01:20,205
[mysterious music]

25
00:01:22,749 --> 00:01:25,294
♪ Lost in the unknown,
so much to see ♪

26
00:01:25,377 --> 00:01:28,589
♪ Together we will rise ♪

27
00:01:28,672 --> 00:01:31,633
♪ We fight ♪

28
00:01:31,717 --> 00:01:36,138
♪ Be a ninja for what's right ♪

29
00:01:36,221 --> 00:01:37,681
[air whooshes]

30
00:01:37,890 --> 00:01:40,684
[suspenseful music]

31
00:01:41,768 --> 00:01:43,729
[footsteps tapping]

32
00:01:43,812 --> 00:01:47,524
[suspenseful music]

33
00:01:47,608 --> 00:01:49,443
You think this junk still works?

34
00:01:49,526 --> 00:01:54,031
Cease the doubting, it will.
[laughing maniacally]

35
00:01:57,701 --> 00:01:59,328
[electricity zapping]

36
00:01:59,411 --> 00:02:02,122
[robot humming]

37
00:02:04,082 --> 00:02:06,793
-[fireball thuds]
-Eat fire, you no-gooders!

38
00:02:06,877 --> 00:02:10,130
The Red Ninja's here
to kick your butts!

39
00:02:10,214 --> 00:02:14,092
Well, Red Ninja-ish.
Meet Wyldfyre!

40
00:02:14,176 --> 00:02:15,761
-[suspenseful music]
-[fireball whooshes]

41
00:02:15,844 --> 00:02:19,640
[suspenseful music]

42
00:02:19,723 --> 00:02:22,351
[fireballs whooshing]

43
00:02:25,145 --> 00:02:26,605
Oh, whoa.

44
00:02:26,688 --> 00:02:29,233
[suspenseful music]

45
00:02:29,316 --> 00:02:30,984
Get back here!

46
00:02:31,068 --> 00:02:33,570
Maybe Kreel will like these
mechs better all burnt up.

47
00:02:33,654 --> 00:02:35,572
[suspenseful music]

48
00:02:35,656 --> 00:02:38,367
[fireballs whooshing]

49
00:02:39,868 --> 00:02:43,372
-[Nya] Ninja go!
-[air whooshing]

50
00:02:50,337 --> 00:02:52,339
Nya, so glad you're here!

51
00:02:52,422 --> 00:02:54,758
Not that I needed help.
Uh... I didn't!

52
00:02:54,842 --> 00:02:57,261
[fireballs whooshing]

53
00:02:57,344 --> 00:03:02,474
[water whooshing]

54
00:03:02,558 --> 00:03:04,768
Oh, yikes, a real Ninja!

55
00:03:04,852 --> 00:03:06,603
Let us flee!

56
00:03:06,687 --> 00:03:08,272
That hurt my feelings!

57
00:03:08,355 --> 00:03:12,442
-[fireball whooshing]
-[suspenseful music]

58
00:03:12,526 --> 00:03:14,319
I Red Ninja'd!

59
00:03:14,403 --> 00:03:15,737
Kai would be honored
you're trying

60
00:03:15,821 --> 00:03:17,990
to take up the mantle of
the Red Ninja, Wyldfyre.

61
00:03:18,073 --> 00:03:19,032
He should be.

62
00:03:19,116 --> 00:03:20,492
But maybe you should wait

63
00:03:20,576 --> 00:03:22,619
until you get
a little more training.

64
00:03:22,703 --> 00:03:24,621
You haven't mastered
Spinjitzu yet,

65
00:03:24,705 --> 00:03:27,040
and I'd hate to
see you get hurt.

66
00:03:27,124 --> 00:03:28,834
Wyldfyre does not get hurt!

67
00:03:28,917 --> 00:03:30,544
You were on a crutch for weeks.

68
00:03:30,627 --> 00:03:33,422
I mean, I don't
get hurt anymore.

69
00:03:33,505 --> 00:03:34,756
Hasn't Lloyd been teaching you

70
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:36,508
to focus more on
your fire precision?

71
00:03:36,592 --> 00:03:39,720
I'm precise.
I'm the most precise!

72
00:03:39,803 --> 00:03:41,346
[robot crashes]

73
00:03:41,430 --> 00:03:44,683
And what about your
weapon training?

74
00:03:44,766 --> 00:03:47,853
There's more to being a
Ninja than Elemental Powers.

75
00:03:47,936 --> 00:03:49,855
I'm the only weapon I need!

76
00:03:49,938 --> 00:03:54,026
Besides, someone has to
carry on Kai's legacy!

77
00:03:54,109 --> 00:03:55,402
It's okay if you miss him.

78
00:03:55,485 --> 00:03:58,488
I do too, more than
you could imagine.

79
00:03:58,572 --> 00:04:00,824
Pfft, I don't miss people.

80
00:04:00,908 --> 00:04:03,368
I'm not emotional like that,

81
00:04:03,452 --> 00:04:07,039
but if I did,
I'd probably miss Kai.

82
00:04:07,664 --> 00:04:09,750
Who knows, maybe
being trapped forever

83
00:04:09,833 --> 00:04:11,960
in the Nether-Space
isn't that bad?

84
00:04:13,253 --> 00:04:16,924
Yeah, I knew that sounded
dumb as soon as I said it.

85
00:04:17,758 --> 00:04:20,636
I just hope it's at least
a peaceful place for Kai.

86
00:04:22,638 --> 00:04:24,556
[suspenseful music]

87
00:04:24,640 --> 00:04:27,309
Ugh, this place is infuriating!
[exhales deeply]

88
00:04:28,435 --> 00:04:29,686
[sighs]

89
00:04:29,770 --> 00:04:31,813
[suspenseful music]

90
00:04:31,897 --> 00:04:33,565
We have to be quiet.

91
00:04:33,649 --> 00:04:35,025
If the rest of
the Forbidden Five

92
00:04:35,108 --> 00:04:36,902
figure out we're trapped
in here with them,

93
00:04:36,985 --> 00:04:39,613
it won't go well.
For us, I mean.

94
00:04:39,696 --> 00:04:41,865
They'd probably
love destroying us.

95
00:04:41,949 --> 00:04:44,201
[suspenseful music]

96
00:04:49,831 --> 00:04:50,749
-[footsteps thudding]
-[Bonzle gasps]

97
00:04:50,832 --> 00:04:52,960
-[ominous music]
-Huh?

98
00:04:54,253 --> 00:04:55,420
I don't think they saw us.

99
00:04:55,504 --> 00:04:56,547
Let's go this way.

100
00:04:57,506 --> 00:04:58,924
Oof!

101
00:04:59,007 --> 00:05:03,428
-[rocks clattering]
-[ominous music]

102
00:05:03,512 --> 00:05:04,972
Maybe they didn't hear us.

103
00:05:05,055 --> 00:05:07,599
[suspenseful music]

104
00:05:07,683 --> 00:05:09,768
-[gasps] They heard us.
-Run!

105
00:05:12,813 --> 00:05:16,066
[door creaks, thuds]

106
00:05:16,149 --> 00:05:18,735
Mm, what's this, new recipe?

107
00:05:18,819 --> 00:05:22,364
New to you:
Merlopian Berry Creme.

108
00:05:22,447 --> 00:05:24,575
My best friend, Frak,
taught me how to make it.

109
00:05:24,658 --> 00:05:26,118
Your best friend?

110
00:05:26,201 --> 00:05:27,619
[Riyu whimpers]

111
00:05:27,703 --> 00:05:29,746
Besides you two, I mean.

112
00:05:29,830 --> 00:05:32,082
Frak was my bestie
before the Merge.

113
00:05:32,165 --> 00:05:34,668
He was as big a ninja fan as me.

114
00:05:34,751 --> 00:05:36,795
Wow, that's saying something.

115
00:05:36,879 --> 00:05:38,881
He'd be so excited for me now.

116
00:05:38,964 --> 00:05:41,717
But he moved away,
and we lost touch.

117
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:43,635
Mm, we'll always have this pie.

118
00:05:43,719 --> 00:05:45,762
[Riyu slurps and gulps]

119
00:05:45,846 --> 00:05:47,681
Okay, then, I'll make more.

120
00:05:49,266 --> 00:05:52,186
I wanna bake everyone
a goodbye treat,

121
00:05:52,269 --> 00:05:54,646
before you all head off to
the Tournament of the Sources.

122
00:05:54,730 --> 00:05:57,691
"Goodbye treat?"
　You're coming with us, right?

123
00:05:57,774 --> 00:06:00,819
The Tournament is for
Masters of Elemental Powers.

124
00:06:00,903 --> 00:06:02,988
You know, the kind of
powers I don't have?

125
00:06:03,071 --> 00:06:05,824
You're the Elemental
Master of Pie!

126
00:06:05,908 --> 00:06:07,659
Seriously, though,
you have to come.

127
00:06:07,743 --> 00:06:08,660
You're part of the team.

128
00:06:08,744 --> 00:06:10,078
It sounds amazing,

129
00:06:10,162 --> 00:06:13,916
but there's no place
for me there, Sora.

130
00:06:13,999 --> 00:06:16,960
-[wings flapping]
-[suspenseful music]

131
00:06:17,044 --> 00:06:19,004
[Motion Dragon]
If you are going to enter

132
00:06:19,087 --> 00:06:20,756
the Tournament of the Sources

133
00:06:20,839 --> 00:06:24,092
to find the villain
behind these attacks,

134
00:06:24,176 --> 00:06:29,765
I'd advise you all to find
a Master to lead you.

135
00:06:29,848 --> 00:06:33,018
-[wings whooshing]
-[mysterious music]

136
00:06:33,101 --> 00:06:34,978
[feet thud]

137
00:06:35,062 --> 00:06:37,731
[mysterious music]

138
00:06:39,399 --> 00:06:41,777
[wings whooshing]

139
00:06:41,860 --> 00:06:44,821
Egalt, Rontu,
I've come for Zane.

140
00:06:44,905 --> 00:06:47,366
Oh, and Wyldfyre wanted
me to give you this,

141
00:06:47,449 --> 00:06:48,742
Janus Melon Stew.

142
00:06:50,577 --> 00:06:52,663
[Egalt sniffs]

143
00:06:52,746 --> 00:06:57,543
Mm, that was quite kind of her.

144
00:06:57,626 --> 00:07:00,170
[suspenseful music]

145
00:07:01,588 --> 00:07:03,131
Zane! [chuckles]

146
00:07:04,216 --> 00:07:06,134
-[Zane yelps]
-Good to see you, too.

147
00:07:06,343 --> 00:07:08,387
[Zane yelps]

148
00:07:08,470 --> 00:07:10,681
I am in a training
exercise, Lloyd!

149
00:07:10,764 --> 00:07:12,224
[suspenseful music]

150
00:07:12,307 --> 00:07:13,725
[wings whooshing]

151
00:07:13,809 --> 00:07:18,689
[Zane yelping]

152
00:07:18,772 --> 00:07:20,649
[suspenseful music]

153
00:07:20,899 --> 00:07:22,317
-[rocks thudding]
-[Zane grunts]

154
00:07:22,401 --> 00:07:24,319
-[air whooshes]
-[rocks thudding]

155
00:07:24,403 --> 00:07:27,155
You're too focused
on fighting back!

156
00:07:27,239 --> 00:07:29,533
Try to harmonize with
the motion of the rocks!

157
00:07:29,741 --> 00:07:32,119
-[air whooshing]
-[Zane yelps]

158
00:07:32,202 --> 00:07:35,372
[suspenseful music]

159
00:07:36,790 --> 00:07:37,833
[Zane grunts]

160
00:07:38,667 --> 00:07:40,794
[air whooshing]

161
00:07:45,299 --> 00:07:46,508
[body crashes]

162
00:07:46,592 --> 00:07:48,969
[suspenseful music]

163
00:07:49,178 --> 00:07:52,931
You did it! You mastered
Rising Dragon Technique!

164
00:07:53,015 --> 00:07:55,642
Your last-minute guidance
was most welcome.

165
00:07:55,726 --> 00:07:58,812
[Egalt] Despite
my initial misgivings,

166
00:07:58,896 --> 00:08:03,442
all you Ninja have proven
yourselves to be true masters.

167
00:08:03,525 --> 00:08:05,110
I just hope my Rising Dragon

168
00:08:05,194 --> 00:08:07,988
is enough to combat
Shatterspin technique.

169
00:08:08,071 --> 00:08:10,908
Well, now that you, me,
Kai, and Nya can do it,

170
00:08:10,991 --> 00:08:12,284
at least we stand a chance

171
00:08:12,367 --> 00:08:14,494
if we ever run into
Ras and his crew again.

172
00:08:14,578 --> 00:08:17,039
But we have more
pressing problems now.

173
00:08:17,247 --> 00:08:19,583
Someone killed the Matriarch
of the Mountain Dragons

174
00:08:19,666 --> 00:08:21,001
and stole her horns.

175
00:08:21,084 --> 00:08:23,462
They did the same
to two other dragons.

176
00:08:23,545 --> 00:08:25,339
Why would someone
do such a thing?

177
00:08:25,422 --> 00:08:27,090
We don't know.

178
00:08:27,174 --> 00:08:29,051
But the Motion Source
Dragon came to us for help.

179
00:08:29,134 --> 00:08:31,011
She fears whoever did this

180
00:08:31,094 --> 00:08:33,055
is coming for the
Source Dragons next.

181
00:08:33,138 --> 00:08:34,848
There must be grave danger

182
00:08:34,932 --> 00:08:37,434
for a Source Dragon
to ask for aid.

183
00:08:37,518 --> 00:08:40,020
If the Source Dragons
are destroyed,

184
00:08:40,103 --> 00:08:42,147
it could mean
the end of everything.

185
00:08:42,231 --> 00:08:43,732
Are there any suspects?

186
00:08:43,815 --> 00:08:46,401
No, but we believe
whoever did it

187
00:08:46,485 --> 00:08:48,779
is entering the
Tournament of the Sources,

188
00:08:48,862 --> 00:08:50,197
which is why I'm here.

189
00:08:51,532 --> 00:08:56,453
For most of my life, we had
a great master, Master Wu,

190
00:08:57,246 --> 00:08:59,206
but we lost him in the Merge.

191
00:08:59,289 --> 00:09:01,875
He disappeared or worse.

192
00:09:04,002 --> 00:09:05,879
So I'm formally asking,

193
00:09:05,963 --> 00:09:09,174
will you be our Masters in
the Tournament of the Sources?

194
00:09:09,258 --> 00:09:10,801
-[suspenseful music]
-No.

195
00:09:10,884 --> 00:09:12,970
Thank you. What?

196
00:09:13,053 --> 00:09:15,597
[Egalt] We have nothing
more to teach you.

197
00:09:16,473 --> 00:09:20,477
You, Lloyd, must be
the one to lead the Ninja.

198
00:09:21,603 --> 00:09:23,105
It is your duty.

199
00:09:23,188 --> 00:09:26,233
-But I'm no Master.
-No?

200
00:09:27,192 --> 00:09:28,318
No!

201
00:09:29,111 --> 00:09:30,612
-[Egalt roars]
-What are you doing?

202
00:09:30,696 --> 00:09:33,156
-[foot thuds]
-[Lloyd panting]

203
00:09:33,240 --> 00:09:34,700
[Zane yelps]

204
00:09:34,783 --> 00:09:37,953
[suspenseful music]

205
00:09:38,036 --> 00:09:39,705
-[Lloyd grunts]
-[wing crashes]

206
00:09:41,081 --> 00:09:43,667
[Lloyd yelps]

207
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:45,961
[tail crashes]

208
00:09:46,044 --> 00:09:47,212
[Lloyd grunting]

209
00:09:47,296 --> 00:09:48,380
[suspenseful music]

210
00:09:48,463 --> 00:09:52,050
-[air whooshing]
-[Lloyd grunts]

211
00:09:55,137 --> 00:09:57,723
You just beat two
of the greatest warriors

212
00:09:57,806 --> 00:09:59,349
that ever lived.

213
00:10:00,017 --> 00:10:02,352
Granted,
we are not in our prime.

214
00:10:02,436 --> 00:10:04,271
Now give me that stew.

215
00:10:08,192 --> 00:10:09,943
You didn't spill a drop.

216
00:10:10,027 --> 00:10:12,613
[slurping] Excellent.

217
00:10:12,696 --> 00:10:16,867
You passed our test,
Master Lloyd.

218
00:10:16,950 --> 00:10:19,077
[mysterious music]

219
00:10:19,161 --> 00:10:21,830
My Master Wu was a true Master.

220
00:10:21,914 --> 00:10:23,123
I'm not ready.

221
00:10:23,832 --> 00:10:26,960
You've faced much
in your young life

222
00:10:27,044 --> 00:10:28,921
and have lost much--

223
00:10:29,004 --> 00:10:33,592
your master,
teammates, friends--

224
00:10:33,675 --> 00:10:35,177
and because of that,

225
00:10:35,260 --> 00:10:38,680
you fear you won't be
able to protect everybody.

226
00:10:38,764 --> 00:10:41,308
Your heart is too big, Lloyd.

227
00:10:41,391 --> 00:10:45,145
Which is exactly why
you must lead the Ninja.

228
00:10:45,229 --> 00:10:47,314
It is why you are
the one to carry on

229
00:10:47,397 --> 00:10:50,234
the legacy of your
beloved Master Wu.

230
00:10:50,317 --> 00:10:53,779
But what if I face
a problem I can't handle?

231
00:10:53,862 --> 00:10:55,197
What if I fail?

232
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:56,698
We have faith you will

233
00:10:56,782 --> 00:10:59,576
rise to the challenge,
Master Lloyd.

234
00:11:00,452 --> 00:11:02,538
You always do.

235
00:11:02,621 --> 00:11:05,123
Is this really necessary?

236
00:11:05,207 --> 00:11:06,583
The Dragon Masters showed me

237
00:11:06,667 --> 00:11:08,961
there are benefits
of stew-jitzu.

238
00:11:10,212 --> 00:11:12,339
Huh, get it?

239
00:11:12,422 --> 00:11:13,882
Ugh.

240
00:11:13,966 --> 00:11:15,467
Come on, let's go!

241
00:11:15,551 --> 00:11:19,555
-[air whooshing]
-[suspenseful music]

242
00:11:20,639 --> 00:11:21,807
[whimsical music]

243
00:11:21,890 --> 00:11:24,935
[slurping] What?

244
00:11:25,018 --> 00:11:26,979
I like what I like:
stew.

245
00:11:27,062 --> 00:11:28,313
[Riyu slurping]

246
00:11:30,357 --> 00:11:33,235
So, Lloyd, I just wanted
to tell you, the tournament.

247
00:11:33,318 --> 00:11:37,531
I, uh, I'm not gonna go.
I don't have an Elemental Power.

248
00:11:37,614 --> 00:11:40,367
Arin, we're not going to
the tournament to win.

249
00:11:40,450 --> 00:11:43,328
-We're not?
-Well, unless we have to win

250
00:11:43,412 --> 00:11:45,664
to bring the Matriarch's
attacker to justice.

251
00:11:45,747 --> 00:11:48,417
Someone killed those dragons
and stole their horns.

252
00:11:48,500 --> 00:11:51,587
It's up to us
to find out who and why.

253
00:11:51,670 --> 00:11:54,173
Which means you might have
the most important job of all.

254
00:11:54,256 --> 00:11:56,717
To solve the mystery
while you all compete?

255
00:11:56,800 --> 00:12:00,179
Exactly. The Motion
Dragon is relying on us,

256
00:12:00,262 --> 00:12:02,431
and I'm relying on you, Arin.

257
00:12:02,514 --> 00:12:05,184
Okay, that I can do.

258
00:12:05,267 --> 00:12:07,686
My parents were
huge mystery fans,

259
00:12:07,769 --> 00:12:09,396
always reading detective books,

260
00:12:09,479 --> 00:12:11,648
teaching me how
investigations work.

261
00:12:11,732 --> 00:12:12,983
This is all me...

262
00:12:14,193 --> 00:12:16,987
and now I won't feel so
useless at the tournament.

263
00:12:17,070 --> 00:12:19,072
You're never useless, Arin.

264
00:12:19,156 --> 00:12:20,199
Now get packing.

265
00:12:20,282 --> 00:12:22,159
It's time for us to go.

266
00:12:22,242 --> 00:12:26,914
[mysterious music]

267
00:12:29,374 --> 00:12:32,836
[engine roaring]

268
00:12:37,174 --> 00:12:39,009
[grunts] We're here.

269
00:12:39,092 --> 00:12:40,844
According to the
Motion Source Dragon,

270
00:12:41,053 --> 00:12:43,931
that waterfall is the way
to the tournament somehow.

271
00:12:44,932 --> 00:12:48,060
We're gonna meet all kinds
of new Elemental Masters!

272
00:12:48,143 --> 00:12:50,062
Ah, this is gonna be so cool.

273
00:12:50,145 --> 00:12:53,232
Remember, not every
Master is an ally.

274
00:12:53,315 --> 00:12:56,109
-Cinder could be here, or--
-Euphrasia.

275
00:12:56,193 --> 00:13:00,322
Yes, she might be here,
but she is our friend.

276
00:13:00,405 --> 00:13:02,157
I am only listing enemies.

277
00:13:02,241 --> 00:13:03,158
Not might be.

278
00:13:03,242 --> 00:13:05,661
She is here, look!

279
00:13:05,744 --> 00:13:07,412
[air whooshing]

280
00:13:07,871 --> 00:13:09,122
[suspenseful music]

281
00:13:09,206 --> 00:13:12,334
-[slot rumbles]
-[scroll clinks]

282
00:13:12,417 --> 00:13:15,546
[door rumbles]

283
00:13:15,629 --> 00:13:18,632
[suspenseful music]

284
00:13:23,428 --> 00:13:24,805
[Cole] Whoa!

285
00:13:24,888 --> 00:13:27,724
[squeals] Could
this get any cooler?

286
00:13:27,808 --> 00:13:29,893
And you were thinking
about not even coming.

287
00:13:29,977 --> 00:13:31,311
Let's go.

288
00:13:38,026 --> 00:13:40,195
[Nya] Guess the tournament
is on top of that cliff?

289
00:13:40,279 --> 00:13:42,406
So, let's do this.

290
00:13:42,489 --> 00:13:44,241
Uh, how do we do this?

291
00:13:44,324 --> 00:13:45,576
[mysterious music]

292
00:13:46,743 --> 00:13:48,370
Take us to the tournament!

293
00:13:51,540 --> 00:13:52,583
Please?

294
00:13:55,544 --> 00:13:59,339
Euphrasia put something
in here, some kind of scroll.

295
00:13:59,423 --> 00:14:00,674
Hey, look at this!

296
00:14:01,383 --> 00:14:04,553
Hello, can anyone hear me?

297
00:14:04,636 --> 00:14:06,555
[mysterious music]

298
00:14:06,638 --> 00:14:09,850
We are here for the tournament!

299
00:14:09,933 --> 00:14:14,563
[door rumbling]

300
00:14:16,899 --> 00:14:21,570
Hello, I am Bleckt,
Minister of Ledgering

301
00:14:21,653 --> 00:14:24,281
for the Tournament
of the Sources.

302
00:14:24,364 --> 00:14:27,201
Great, and you're in charge
of the guest list, sir?

303
00:14:27,284 --> 00:14:32,289
Not just the guest list,
all lists, tabulations,

304
00:14:32,372 --> 00:14:35,334
Itineraries, agendas,
and inventories

305
00:14:35,417 --> 00:14:39,421
fall under my duties
with the ledger.

306
00:14:39,505 --> 00:14:41,048
The tournament has been run

307
00:14:41,131 --> 00:14:44,676
by my family for
generations untold.

308
00:14:44,760 --> 00:14:49,056
For each tournament, our city
would rotate to another Realm,

309
00:14:49,139 --> 00:14:53,185
and invitations would go
out by spirit dragon courier

310
00:14:53,268 --> 00:14:56,605
to all Elemental Masters there.

311
00:14:56,688 --> 00:14:59,691
Although now all
the Elemental Masters

312
00:14:59,775 --> 00:15:02,319
are in the same Merged Lands.

313
00:15:02,402 --> 00:15:06,532
So more invitations have
gone out than ever before.

314
00:15:06,615 --> 00:15:11,078
Well, it appears your spirit
dragons didn't get to us.

315
00:15:11,161 --> 00:15:15,207
Oh, well, there's a simple
solution to that.

316
00:15:15,290 --> 00:15:16,708
Great, 'cause I was afraid

317
00:15:16,792 --> 00:15:18,126
this was gonna be a whole thing.

318
00:15:18,210 --> 00:15:22,464
The solution is you go away.

319
00:15:22,548 --> 00:15:26,802
If you didn't get an invitation,
you are not invited.

320
00:15:26,885 --> 00:15:30,639
My dude, we're definitely
esteemed Elemental Masters,

321
00:15:30,722 --> 00:15:32,474
so we must be invited.

322
00:15:32,558 --> 00:15:34,518
Please don't make a fuss.

323
00:15:34,601 --> 00:15:36,436
From the look of you,

324
00:15:36,520 --> 00:15:39,398
you wouldn't be up to the
challenge of the games anyway.

325
00:15:39,481 --> 00:15:42,693
Whoa, who are you, the
Elemental Master of Shade?

326
00:15:42,776 --> 00:15:46,572
No, that's the Elemental
Master of Shade.

327
00:15:48,156 --> 00:15:50,534
Welcome, Mistress Obscuria!

328
00:15:50,617 --> 00:15:52,744
See you in the City of Temples.

329
00:15:52,828 --> 00:15:55,539
[door rumbles]

330
00:15:56,498 --> 00:15:58,458
[mysterious music]

331
00:15:58,542 --> 00:16:02,921
Now please leave
and stop wasting my time.

332
00:16:03,005 --> 00:16:04,965
[door closes loudly]

333
00:16:05,048 --> 00:16:07,676
Oh, man, I was
really hoping to see

334
00:16:07,759 --> 00:16:09,219
who's at the tournament.

335
00:16:09,303 --> 00:16:11,430
We're not done yet.

336
00:16:11,513 --> 00:16:14,433
[suspenseful music]

337
00:16:22,482 --> 00:16:24,484
[slot rumbles]

338
00:16:24,568 --> 00:16:25,694
[scroll clinks]

339
00:16:26,695 --> 00:16:28,197
[air whooshes]

340
00:16:30,157 --> 00:16:31,408
[Nya] Now!

341
00:16:31,491 --> 00:16:34,912
[suspenseful music]

342
00:16:37,080 --> 00:16:39,416
[metal clangs]

343
00:16:40,501 --> 00:16:42,419
[tires screeching]

344
00:16:44,630 --> 00:16:49,468
[Arin] We're doing it!
I knew we'd find a way-- [yelps]

345
00:16:49,551 --> 00:16:51,803
Warning, warning,
intruder alert!

346
00:16:51,887 --> 00:16:54,681
[Zane] This situation
is less than optimal.

347
00:16:55,724 --> 00:16:58,477
[guns firing]

348
00:17:00,187 --> 00:17:01,855
[Wyldfyre] We're intruders?

349
00:17:01,939 --> 00:17:06,360
You're intruding
on our intrusion! Eat fire!

350
00:17:06,985 --> 00:17:08,779
Uninvited guests
are not permitted

351
00:17:08,862 --> 00:17:11,073
in the City of Temples.

352
00:17:11,156 --> 00:17:15,911
-[guns firing]
-[suspenseful music]

353
00:17:16,828 --> 00:17:18,830
[Arin] Abandon
ship, or, uh, car!

354
00:17:18,914 --> 00:17:21,583
-[guns firing]
-[Sora grunts]

355
00:17:21,667 --> 00:17:24,461
[Security Bot] This unit
has an unauthorized rider!

356
00:17:24,545 --> 00:17:27,422
[suspenseful music]

357
00:17:27,506 --> 00:17:31,635
[Arin] Hey, whoa!

358
00:17:41,061 --> 00:17:43,647
Let's see how you like
an Elemental tech remix!

359
00:17:45,691 --> 00:17:47,901
-[Sora yelping]
-[air whooshing]

360
00:17:47,985 --> 00:17:51,113
[grunts] Great,
their tech must be so old,

361
00:17:51,196 --> 00:17:53,490
my powers don't work
on it or something.

362
00:17:53,574 --> 00:17:55,784
[air whooshing]

363
00:18:01,832 --> 00:18:04,251
[stones crunching]

364
00:18:04,334 --> 00:18:09,298
-[guns firing]
-[Jiro roaring]

365
00:18:09,381 --> 00:18:11,258
[Lloyd] Sounds
like a plan, Jiro!

366
00:18:11,341 --> 00:18:13,719
Off the dragons, onto
the wall, everyone!

367
00:18:14,803 --> 00:18:19,850
-[air whooshing]
-[suspenseful music]

368
00:18:29,067 --> 00:18:31,069
Looks like we have to climb
the rest of the way up.

369
00:18:31,153 --> 00:18:32,946
[Wyldfyre gasps]

370
00:18:33,989 --> 00:18:37,326
-Oh, no, I'm gonna barf.
-You ride dragons.

371
00:18:37,409 --> 00:18:39,161
How are you possibly
afraid of heights?

372
00:18:39,244 --> 00:18:40,621
Dragons are the safest

373
00:18:40,704 --> 00:18:42,915
and most solid thing
to stand on ever!

374
00:18:42,998 --> 00:18:44,458
This is not!

375
00:18:44,541 --> 00:18:46,251
[air whooshes]

376
00:18:46,335 --> 00:18:48,921
Arin, Arin, has
anyone seen Arin?

377
00:18:50,130 --> 00:18:51,673
I thought I saw him hitch
a ride straight to the top

378
00:18:51,757 --> 00:18:53,509
on one of those flying bots.

379
00:18:53,592 --> 00:18:54,676
Riyu went after him.

380
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:56,595
I hope he's okay.

381
00:18:56,678 --> 00:18:57,888
[metal clangs]

382
00:19:03,227 --> 00:19:05,354
[grunts]

383
00:19:05,437 --> 00:19:07,564
[panting, grunting]

384
00:19:09,358 --> 00:19:11,568
[suspenseful music]

385
00:19:11,652 --> 00:19:14,029
-[Spectator 1] Hey!
-[Spectator 2, laughing]
Whoo-hoo!

386
00:19:14,112 --> 00:19:16,448
[Spectator 1] Yeah, ha!

387
00:19:16,532 --> 00:19:17,991
People are watching us?

388
00:19:21,620 --> 00:19:22,663
[door rumbles]

389
00:19:22,746 --> 00:19:23,997
[Sora] The gates!

390
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:29,670
-[Roby vocalizing]
-Your arrival was--

391
00:19:29,753 --> 00:19:33,006
Awesome, incredible,
massively driving engagement!

392
00:19:33,090 --> 00:19:37,010
-Undignified!
-Are you kidding?

393
00:19:37,094 --> 00:19:39,388
Sure, it was different
than the other competitors,

394
00:19:39,471 --> 00:19:42,182
which is exactly
what these games need!

395
00:19:42,266 --> 00:19:44,601
These Ninja are disruptors!

396
00:19:44,685 --> 00:19:48,021
Disruption does not impress me.

397
00:19:48,105 --> 00:19:51,984
Ugh, Uncle Bleckt, it's time
to shake this tournament up!

398
00:19:52,067 --> 00:19:55,696
We've established millennia
of sacred traditions!

399
00:19:55,779 --> 00:19:58,907
We do not shake anything up!

400
00:19:58,991 --> 00:20:00,951
Guards, arrest them!

401
00:20:01,034 --> 00:20:04,538
[suspenseful music]

402
00:20:04,621 --> 00:20:07,958
Uh, uh, uh, who's
in charge here?

403
00:20:09,084 --> 00:20:12,087
Who is in charge here, that kid?

404
00:20:12,921 --> 00:20:16,383
Great to meet you! I'm Roby,
the new Master of Ceremonies

405
00:20:16,466 --> 00:20:17,926
of the Tournament of Sources.

406
00:20:18,010 --> 00:20:20,304
No big deal, but this
is kind of my event now,

407
00:20:20,387 --> 00:20:21,805
and it's a big deal.

408
00:20:21,889 --> 00:20:23,849
My folks retired to
the Kingdom of Madness.

409
00:20:23,932 --> 00:20:26,560
There are amazing deals
on real estate there right now.

410
00:20:26,643 --> 00:20:27,936
They couldn't pass it up.

411
00:20:28,020 --> 00:20:29,813
And they left this
tournament to me.

412
00:20:29,897 --> 00:20:32,774
Your uncle doesn't seem
too pleased about that fact.

413
00:20:32,858 --> 00:20:36,153
Yeah, Uncle Bleckt
is a bit of um, mm--

414
00:20:36,236 --> 00:20:37,905
Wet dragon tail?

415
00:20:37,988 --> 00:20:42,451
If that's your cute way of
saying stick in the mud, 100%.

416
00:20:42,534 --> 00:20:44,953
And I have big plans
to update this tournament.

417
00:20:45,037 --> 00:20:48,749
Consider me the Elemental
Master of Surprise!

418
00:20:48,832 --> 00:20:50,542
J-K, J-K, J-K.

419
00:20:50,626 --> 00:20:52,377
Anyway, this year
is just the beginning

420
00:20:52,461 --> 00:20:53,879
of what's gonna
become a multi-media,

421
00:20:53,962 --> 00:20:56,590
cross-platform content
generating event,

422
00:20:56,673 --> 00:21:00,469
and you, my Ninja, are
now part of my plan.

423
00:21:00,552 --> 00:21:02,095
Don't know what happened
to your invitations,

424
00:21:02,179 --> 00:21:04,765
but you are officially
invited by me,

425
00:21:04,848 --> 00:21:07,100
the Roby himself, to compete.

426
00:21:07,184 --> 00:21:08,894
Welcome to the tournament!

427
00:21:08,977 --> 00:21:10,604
Bah-bah, bah-bah, bah-bah!

428
00:21:10,687 --> 00:21:15,943
-Now behold the City of Temples!
-[Wyldfyre gasps]

429
00:21:16,026 --> 00:21:19,696
A mix of retro
and new, cool, right?

430
00:21:19,780 --> 00:21:21,615
And the games
haven't even started!

431
00:21:21,698 --> 00:21:23,617
Got some big
surprises for later.

432
00:21:23,700 --> 00:21:24,993
This is incredible and all,

433
00:21:25,077 --> 00:21:27,162
but we've got a bigger problem.

434
00:21:27,246 --> 00:21:28,956
Where are Arin and Riyu?

435
00:21:29,039 --> 00:21:31,834
-[flashlight humming]
-[Riyu whimpers]

436
00:21:31,917 --> 00:21:33,877
This is all just
a misunderstanding!

437
00:21:33,961 --> 00:21:36,255
Our invitations
got lost, I swear!

438
00:21:36,338 --> 00:21:38,757
[Frak] Arin, is that you?!

439
00:21:39,508 --> 00:21:40,801
[Arin] Frak?

440
00:21:40,884 --> 00:21:42,970
Oh-ho, it is you!

441
00:21:43,053 --> 00:21:45,347
I haven't seen you
since before the Merge!

442
00:21:46,306 --> 00:21:49,893
[upbeat music playing]

